# BANNED PATTERNS
# Idris2: believe_me, assert_total, assert_smaller, unsafePerformIO
# Haskell: unsafeCoerce, unsafePerformIO, undefined, error
# OCaml: Obj.magic, Obj.repr, Obj.obj
# Coq: Admitted
# Lean: sorry
# Rust: transmute (unless FFI with a // SAFETY: comment)

# FORMAL VERIFICATION — Idris2 ONLY
# standards/0-canon/rsr/LANGUAGE-POLICY.adoc v1.6.0: "Idris2 — Formal
# verification (sole option). Idris2 is the only formal-verification language.
# ATS2 is rejected." There is a narrow Coq-only carve-out and NONE for Agda,
# Lean4 or TLA+.
#
# verification/proofs/ currently carries agda/, lean4/ and tlaplus/ in
# violation of that policy. Do not add to them; write new proofs in
# verification/proofs/idris2/.

# LANGUAGES — allowed
# AffineScript, Rust/SPARK, Zig, Idris2, Bun, Gleam, Elixir, OCaml, Ada
# (legacy), Haskell, Julia, A2ML, Guile Scheme (build tooling only), Nickel,
# Bash/POSIX shell.

# LANGUAGES — banned
# TypeScript, ReScript, Node.js, npm/yarn, Deno, Go, Python, Java/Kotlin,
# Swift, Flutter/Dart, React Native, V-lang, ATS2.
#
# NOTE: Deno moved from tier 1 to BANNED on 2026-09-22 (policy v1.6.0) and Bun
# is now tier 1. rsr-template-repo/.clinerules still says the opposite — that
# file is stale. This file follows the current ruling.

# CONTAINERS
# Runtime: Podman first. File: Containerfile (never Dockerfile).
# Base: cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base or cgr.dev/chainguard/static.
# Non-root only. Health endpoints /health and /ready stay public.

# ABI/FFI
# ABI: Idris2 with dependent types (src/interface/Abi/).
# FFI: Zig with C ABI (src/interface/ffi/).
# The Rust core links against libpt.a, built by `zig build` in
# src/interface/ffi/ — `cargo test` fails without it.

# BUILD: Use just (Justfile) for all tasks.
# STYLE: Descriptive names. Document all files. SPDX headers everywhere.
# HONESTY: Never claim a test count you have not run. Report faithfully.
